\id GEN
\h Genesis
\toc1 The Book of Genesis
\mt1 Genesis
\rem Fixture: fires every wire code the goldens pin.
\rem 1:3 carries one NO-BREAK SPACE (hygiene). 1:5 and 3:2 hold the only two
\rem straight apostrophes in the corpus, against 59 curly ones (rarity).
\rem 2:4 writes `the the` (doubled) among 438 free uses of `the`; 2:11
\rem capitalizes one of them (casing). 3:7 opens lowercase where every
\rem other verse opens with a capital after a full stop (sentence start).
\rem GEN-edited.usfm is this file with one word of 2:9 changed, and nothing
\rem else: the keystroke the edit golden pins.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 The well wind’s of the basket and the flint beside the net in the dove.
\v 2 The dove rope’s of the flint and the wind beside the dawn in the cloak.
\v 3 The  cedar quail dust’s of the salt and the sickle beside the salt in the seed.
\v 4 The harvest dust fish’s of the fig and the hillside beside the water in the river.
\v 5 The staff salt's jar of the bread and the valley beside the wall in the meadow.
\v 6 The water cloud’s stone of the sand and the clay beside the sheep in the field.
\v 7 The gate staff’s of the cloud and the wind beside the valley in the rope.
\v 8 The basket ash’s pine vine of the staff and the tower beside the hillside in the dawn.
\v 9 The dawn pine’s of the field and the rain beside the river in the pine.
\v 10 The seed stone flint’s wine of the sheep and the furrow beside the wall in the bread.
\v 11 The ash flame’s sheep field of the light and the knife beside the gate in the well.
\v 12 The well fig sand’s hillside of the hillside and the wool beside the goat in the wick.
\v 13 The pine net’s of the net and the linen beside the olive in the oil.
\v 14 The salt spring’s of the cedar and the goat beside the olive in the thread.
\v 15 The wine seed’s of the goat and the dust beside the wine in the quail.
\v 16 The sand light’s dust vine of the wick and the hillside beside the field in the harvest.
\v 17 The sheep basket’s lamp flame of the briar and the furrow beside the ash in the thorn.
\v 18 The orchard rain seed’s wind of the clay and the dye beside the dust in the salt.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 The cloud rain’s of the dawn and the meadow beside the light in the rain.
\v 2 The seed dye’s of the thorn and the linen beside the salt in the harvest.
\v 3 The water ash’s sickle stone of the knife and the sheep beside the furrow in the valley.
\v 4 The dust cedar’s of the field and the flint beside the dove in the the light.
\v 5 The grain goat well’s of the fig and the hillside beside the road in the salt.
\v 6 The dawn ember’s goat of the tower and the pasture beside the plough in the wind.
\v 7 The field plough’s tower brick of the meadow and the bread beside the rain in the yoke.
\v 8 The stone light’s of the well and the rope beside the ox in the stone.
\v 9 The wellspring cloud’s of the dust and the linen beside the dye in the pine.
\v 10 The thread stone’s of the wick and the lamp beside the road in the wind.
\v 11 The cloud beam’s of the brick and the olive beside The fig in the wick.
\v 12 The flint brick’s of the beam and the cedar beside the valley in the olive.
\v 13 The brick lamp’s olive dove of the net and the shore beside the dove in the cedar.
\v 14 The stone clay’s yoke of the dawn and the jar beside the sandal in the ash.
\v 15 The plough knife salt flame’s of the dawn and the well beside the stone in the salt.
\v 16 The salt cloak’s of the sand and the wine beside the cloak in the linen.
\c 3
\p
\v 1 The clay road orchard’s of the stone and the sandal beside the rain in the gate.
\v 2 The seed ash's thread of the water and the bread beside the clay in the sand.
\v 3 The wall sheep clay’s of the sheep and the quail beside the sheep in the furrow.
\v 4 The oil flame’s linen harvest of the wall and the yoke beside the harvest in the orchard.
\v 5 The pasture fish’s of the shore and the wall beside the sickle in the yoke.
\v 6 The basket dove basket oil’s of the goat and the sand beside the vine in the furrow.
\v 7 the ash bread’s of the well and the wick beside the linen in the pasture.
\v 8 The fish briar jar’s dust of the vine and the ash beside the olive in the cedar.
\v 9 The yoke wine’s beam of the knife and the gate beside the thread in the pine.
\v 10 The jar knife’s plough of the bread and the light beside the flame in the ember.
\v 11 The reed wall’s of the rope and the sheep beside the valley in the harvest.
\v 12 The linen thread’s salt cloak of the bread and the pasture beside the fig in the field.
\v 13 The gate jar’s of the spring and the ember beside the brick in the dawn.
\v 14 The dye field brick’s of the ash and the sandal beside the sand in the sand.
\v 15 The ash road of the hillside and the sheep beside the wine in the clay.
\v 16 The shore lamp jar olive of the ox and the gate beside the orchard in the yoke.
